 "description": "# \n\nTask Description: Problem Statement We have N sticks with negligible thickness.\nThe length of the i-th stick is A_i.\nSnuke wants to select four different sticks from these sticks and form a rectangle (including a square), using the sticks as its sides.\nFind the maximum possible area of the rectangle.\nTask Constraint: 4 <= N <= 10^5\n1 <= A_i <= 10^9\nA_i is an integer.\nTask Input: Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 A_2 . . . A_N\nTask Output: Print the maximum possible area of the rectangle.\nIf no rectangle can be formed, print 0.\nTask Samples: input: 6\n3 1 2 4 2 1 output: 2\n\n1 * 2 rectangle can be formed.\ninput: 4\n1 2 3 4 output: 0\n\nNo rectangle can be formed.\ninput: 10\n3 3 3 3 4 4 4 5 5 5 output: 20\n\n## Constraints\n4 <= N <= 10^5\n1 <= A_i <= 10^9\nA_i is an integer.\n\n## Input\nInput is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 A_2 . . . A_N\n\n## Output\nPrint the maximum possible area of the rectangle.\nIf no rectangle can be formed, print 0.\n\n## Examples\n['input: 6\\n3 1 2 4 2 1 output: 2\\n\\n1 * 2 rectangle can be formed.', 'input: 4\\n1 2 3 4 output: 0\\n\\nNo rectangle can be formed.', 'input: 10\\n3 3 3 3 4 4 4 5 5 5 output: 20']",
